1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Spirits, how do we deal with trans-spatial lifeforms that cause disasters?

2
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:13,000
Strategy 1, destroy them through overwhelming military force.

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Or Strategy 2, date them and make them fall in love.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:45,000
Strategy 2, date them and make them fall in love.

5
00:00:45,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Strategy 2, date them and make them fall in love.

6
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:07,000
Strategy 2, date them and make them fall in love.

7
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:17,000
Comments open再見 2, date them and make them fall out in love.

8
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:24,000
न換 richter time switch.

9
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:53,980
It's pretty simple, Miss Okamine.

10
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:57,360
Yes, I am totally a boy now.

11
00:01:57,460 --> 00:02:00,680
So I can stay in the same room as Shido when we go on the school trip.

12
00:02:00,840 --> 00:02:01,940
I don't think so.

13
00:02:02,060 --> 00:02:06,220
You can keep wearing those clothes, but it doesn't change the fact that boys and girls have to stay in separate rooms.

14
00:02:06,280 --> 00:02:06,840
Excuse me.

15
00:02:07,320 --> 00:02:10,000
I think you should approve Toka's unusual request.

16
00:02:10,600 --> 00:02:11,840
Or at least consider it.

17
00:02:12,200 --> 00:02:12,560
Huh?

18
00:02:13,680 --> 00:02:14,440
Hold on.

19
00:02:14,580 --> 00:02:15,440
What are you after?

20
00:02:15,760 --> 00:02:18,780
I really admire that you have the courage to come out in front of everyone.

21
00:02:19,200 --> 00:02:21,560
I think you deserve to stay in the boys' room, no question.

22
00:02:21,560 --> 00:02:24,800
Look, I'm not saying thanks.

23
00:02:24,940 --> 00:02:25,660
None needed.

24
00:02:25,780 --> 00:02:28,200
Stop wasting time! The issue is not negotiable!

25
00:02:28,580 --> 00:02:32,360
But it is still pretty uncommon for a girl to want to become a boy.

26
00:02:32,560 --> 00:02:35,080
To keep things balanced will make Shido into a girl.

27
00:02:35,260 --> 00:02:36,980
That literally makes no sense.

28
00:02:37,500 --> 00:02:39,400
Then we can bathe together, tastefully.

29
00:02:39,560 --> 00:02:40,680
How's that tasteful?

30
00:02:40,920 --> 00:02:41,620
Wait a sec!

31
00:02:41,620 --> 00:02:45,720
If he becomes a girl, he won't be able to stay in the boys' room with me!

32
00:02:45,880 --> 00:02:47,940
You're a man now. You need to stay strong.

33
00:02:48,220 --> 00:02:50,760
Then this must have been part of your plan all along!

34
00:02:51,840 --> 00:02:53,400
You are both being ridiculous!

35
00:02:53,840 --> 00:02:57,340
Boys and girls will be in separate rooms and no more gender swapping, got it?

36
00:02:57,340 --> 00:03:01,960
Um, well, putting room assignments aside, you can choose your seats for the plane ride.

37
00:03:02,120 --> 00:03:03,440
You can spend time together there!

38
00:03:08,840 --> 00:03:11,000
The location for the school trip?

39
00:03:11,280 --> 00:03:13,020
Yeah, Shido told me about it.

40
00:03:13,360 --> 00:03:15,840
They were going to Okinawa, but now it's a Ruby Island.

41
00:03:16,180 --> 00:03:18,140
We're talking a last-minute change here.

42
00:03:18,140 --> 00:03:23,060
It seems a certain travel agency said they would cover all expenses in order to get publicity shots.

43
00:03:23,500 --> 00:03:26,000
With all financial burden lifted, the school quickly agreed.

44
00:03:26,280 --> 00:03:27,080
However...

45
00:03:27,080 --> 00:03:28,100
Sounds suspicious.

46
00:03:29,040 --> 00:03:31,040
Perhaps I'm reading too much into it.

47
00:03:31,340 --> 00:03:33,100
But the agency Cross Travel?

48
00:03:33,520 --> 00:03:36,200
It's a subsidiary of DEM Industries.

49
00:03:36,640 --> 00:03:38,840
This was her game from the beginning, wasn't it?

50
00:03:38,940 --> 00:03:41,440
You tricked me into the seat furthest from the window!

51
00:03:41,700 --> 00:03:43,020
I won't be fooled again!

52
00:03:43,280 --> 00:03:45,360
You never specified which seat you wanted.

53
00:03:45,360 --> 00:03:47,920
Look, Shido.

54
00:03:48,100 --> 00:03:48,600
I'm sorry.

55
00:03:48,620 --> 00:03:49,240
You can see the horizon.

56
00:03:49,260 --> 00:03:49,780
Super sorry.

57
00:03:49,860 --> 00:03:50,140
Shido!

58
00:03:50,340 --> 00:03:50,840
Triple sorry!

59
00:03:50,840 --> 00:03:51,800
This sight is amazing, too!

60
00:03:52,160 --> 00:03:54,500
Everybody knows the aisle is where the action is!

61
00:03:54,540 --> 00:03:55,280
It's pretty cool.

62
00:03:55,420 --> 00:03:56,740
The clouds look just like a carpet.

63
00:03:56,880 --> 00:03:59,260
Well, if you like carpet, I've got what you want!

64
00:03:59,380 --> 00:04:00,000
Right here!

65
00:04:00,220 --> 00:04:01,140
Look at it, Shido!

66
00:04:01,460 --> 00:04:03,480
If I pretend to nap, maybe they'll stop.

67
00:04:04,880 --> 00:04:06,280
Pardon the candid camera.

68
00:04:07,600 --> 00:04:10,340
But I had to capture such a priceless expression.

69
00:04:10,660 --> 00:04:11,820
Uh, uh-huh.

70
00:04:11,820 --> 00:04:15,500
Shido, who was that?

71
00:04:15,680 --> 00:04:17,500
The teacher introduced her to us earlier.

72
00:04:17,700 --> 00:04:20,700
She's the pro photographer the travel agency sent along with us.

73
00:04:21,560 --> 00:04:22,540
A spirit.

74
00:04:23,520 --> 00:04:24,000
Princess.

75
00:04:24,840 --> 00:04:26,540
Your camera is making me jelly!

76
00:04:26,880 --> 00:04:28,120
It's top of the line!

77
00:04:28,280 --> 00:04:29,420
Must have cost thousands!

78
00:04:29,440 --> 00:04:30,700
That's so lame!

79
00:04:30,860 --> 00:04:32,520
You'd have to drive auto-focus!

80
00:04:32,960 --> 00:04:34,180
Is that like a focal point shutter?

81
00:04:34,280 --> 00:04:38,560
Gentlemen, please put your seats and tray tables in an upright and locked position and prepare for landing.

82
00:04:38,560 --> 00:04:39,180
Wow!

83
00:04:44,900 --> 00:04:45,380
Wow!

84
00:04:46,020 --> 00:04:47,140
No way!

85
00:04:48,140 --> 00:04:49,740
Is that the ocean?

86
00:04:50,460 --> 00:04:52,600
Yeah, I guess this is your first time to see it.

87
00:04:53,040 --> 00:04:53,500
Uh-huh!

88
00:04:53,760 --> 00:04:57,180
The water park we went to with Yoshino and Kotori was amazing!

89
00:04:57,440 --> 00:04:58,860
But this place is even better!

90
00:04:59,020 --> 00:04:59,920
More than you know.

91
00:05:02,660 --> 00:05:03,660
Is something wrong?

92
00:05:04,160 --> 00:05:06,880
God, I feel like someone's watching us.

93
00:05:06,880 --> 00:05:10,180
We'll have them take our luggage to the hotel first, understood?

94
00:05:10,640 --> 00:05:12,240
It was probably just the camera.

95
00:05:15,460 --> 00:05:16,880
Incoming from Adeptus One.

96
00:05:17,180 --> 00:05:18,380
They've reached Arubi Island.

97
00:05:19,460 --> 00:05:20,380
Target confirmed.

98
00:05:20,760 --> 00:05:22,440
Akaru Airport, North District.

99
00:05:22,740 --> 00:05:23,620
Camera number six.

100
00:05:24,300 --> 00:05:25,160
It's Princess, sir.

101
00:05:25,280 --> 00:05:25,880
We found her.

102
00:05:26,320 --> 00:05:27,880
That was anticlimactic.

103
00:05:28,460 --> 00:05:30,200
The girl doesn't look like a spirit.

104
00:05:30,880 --> 00:05:32,360
You must not let your guard down.

105
00:05:33,020 --> 00:05:35,400
Intelligence indicates that she is a spirit.

106
00:05:35,400 --> 00:05:38,620
That alone is reason enough to be on level one alert.

107
00:05:39,080 --> 00:05:39,880
Roger that.

108
00:05:40,200 --> 00:05:41,420
Set alert to level one.

109
00:05:42,700 --> 00:05:45,780
By the way, aren't we supposed to have a wizard on the ground?

110
00:05:46,280 --> 00:05:47,580
All right, class four.

111
00:05:47,900 --> 00:05:48,760
Gather round!

112
00:05:49,620 --> 00:05:50,620
That would be me.

113
00:05:50,740 --> 00:05:51,480
We met earlier.

114
00:05:51,720 --> 00:05:54,900
I'll report back to you later on, but for now, the kids are on the move.

115
00:05:55,100 --> 00:05:55,500
Right!

116
00:05:55,640 --> 00:05:56,260
Come on!

117
00:05:56,500 --> 00:05:58,320
Eyes forward, class four!

118
00:05:58,320 --> 00:06:01,120
Since this is a school trip, we'll start the learning now.

119
00:06:01,400 --> 00:06:03,500
We're heading to the Arubi Island Records office.

120
00:06:03,620 --> 00:06:04,300
How exciting!

121
00:06:04,680 --> 00:06:05,020
Seriously?

122
00:06:05,540 --> 00:06:07,200
It sounds like stupid boring.

123
00:06:07,340 --> 00:06:08,140
Not so lame.

124
00:06:08,480 --> 00:06:09,680
Hey, get it out of the way now.

125
00:06:09,760 --> 00:06:10,500
Have fun later.

126
00:06:11,500 --> 00:06:13,000
Am I right, sexy beast?

127
00:06:13,780 --> 00:06:14,700
Okay, gang.

128
00:06:14,960 --> 00:06:16,300
Everyone, follow the flag!

129
00:06:17,160 --> 00:06:17,780
It's time.

130
00:06:17,940 --> 00:06:19,060
Come on, let's book it.

131
00:06:19,280 --> 00:06:21,260
But I know someone's been spying on us.

132
00:06:21,480 --> 00:06:22,620
Hang on, Toka!

133
00:06:22,620 --> 00:06:23,740
Aw, man!

134
00:06:26,220 --> 00:06:27,560
Adeptus One to Arbitel.

135
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:29,580
Princess has broken off from the group.

136
00:06:29,880 --> 00:06:31,020
Track her movements for me.

137
00:06:32,080 --> 00:06:35,140
Also, activate Ashcroft Beta and set to standby.

138
00:06:35,480 --> 00:06:37,500
Then cut off the island from outside communication.

139
00:06:38,060 --> 00:06:39,400
Be ready to strike at any time.

140
00:06:39,580 --> 00:06:41,020
Hey, you're gonna get left behind.

141
00:06:41,540 --> 00:06:43,360
Shouldn't you be taking pictures of us?

142
00:06:43,360 --> 00:06:43,760
So what?

143
00:06:43,820 --> 00:06:45,440
Did you just come for some photos of the scenery?

144
00:06:45,680 --> 00:06:46,820
That's so lame.

145
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:48,920
No, that's not it at all!

146
00:06:49,100 --> 00:06:49,720
We got it already!

147
00:06:49,720 --> 00:06:50,820
You're working, Ellen!

148
00:06:50,820 --> 00:06:54,540
Being a field agent can be rough.

149
00:06:54,780 --> 00:06:56,840
But these precautions seem a bit extreme.

150
00:06:57,320 --> 00:06:59,480
Spirit or not, she's just a teenage girl.

151
00:07:00,240 --> 00:07:02,260
Once we introduce her to the Bandersnatch Unit,

152
00:07:02,380 --> 00:07:03,940
capturing her will be child's play.

153
00:07:04,100 --> 00:07:05,660
Captain, we've got a problem.

154
00:07:07,900 --> 00:07:08,780
The hell?

155
00:07:11,920 --> 00:07:13,760
Weird, this weather came out of nowhere!

156
00:07:14,240 --> 00:07:16,060
Look, if we don't get out of this storm,

157
00:07:16,120 --> 00:07:17,220
it could get really bad!

158
00:07:17,220 --> 00:07:18,520
Sorry, I ran off.

159
00:07:18,760 --> 00:07:20,500
But I know someone was watching us!

160
00:07:20,500 --> 00:07:21,460
I could feel it!

161
00:07:22,480 --> 00:07:25,360
I bet it was just the locals giving a bunch of annoying students

162
00:07:25,360 --> 00:07:26,120
the stink eye.

163
00:07:26,520 --> 00:07:28,160
Now, which way to the records office?

164
00:07:33,400 --> 00:07:34,460
What's going on?

165
00:07:34,560 --> 00:07:36,320
This came to a head way too quickly!

166
00:07:38,320 --> 00:07:38,760
Shido!

167
00:07:39,140 --> 00:07:39,820
Get down!

168
00:07:39,820 --> 00:07:48,440
Toka!

169
00:07:50,340 --> 00:07:50,580
Taka!

170
00:07:50,620 --> 00:07:51,260
Are you okay?

171
00:07:52,020 --> 00:07:52,580
Uh...

172
00:07:52,580 --> 00:07:53,320
Just my luck.

173
00:07:53,320 --> 00:08:03,880
A spirit? Or the AST?

174
00:08:04,460 --> 00:08:06,380
But the spatial quake alarm never sounded.

175
00:08:23,320 --> 00:08:33,120
Spirits? Two of them?

176
00:08:36,460 --> 00:08:38,620
I can't believe you! Please choose me, darling!

177
00:08:38,720 --> 00:08:40,460
It doesn't matter! Yes, it does!

178
00:08:41,620 --> 00:08:45,940
Well, I'll be going then. This isn't exactly the best timing for a meeting at HQ.

179
00:08:46,620 --> 00:08:50,740
But it's a rare chance for the rounds to meet up in person, so I'm expected to make an appearance.

180
00:08:51,200 --> 00:08:53,040
Go. You may leave it to me, Commander.

181
00:08:53,040 --> 00:08:55,300
Don't worry. You can trust us to hold down the port.

182
00:08:55,760 --> 00:08:57,920
Just promise that you'll hurry back when you're done.

183
00:08:58,220 --> 00:09:01,600
But lo, the unbridled passion of youth set free during a school trip.

184
00:09:01,780 --> 00:09:07,160
And I, Kyohei Kanazuki, will chronicle this page of Shido's salad days with every juicy detail during your absence.

185
00:09:07,340 --> 00:09:09,740
Right. I reiterate. Please hurry back.

186
00:09:10,280 --> 00:09:11,200
Sure. I'll try.

187
00:09:15,780 --> 00:09:21,620
Okay. As acting commander of the mighty Frexinus, flood a course for 15,000 feet above the island.

188
00:09:21,620 --> 00:09:30,540
Not too bad, Yuzuru.

189
00:09:30,880 --> 00:09:33,060
Although I expected as much from my other half.

190
00:09:33,260 --> 00:09:34,840
Too bad it will all have been in vain.

191
00:09:34,960 --> 00:09:37,500
Rebuttal. Much has been learned from our 99 battles.

192
00:09:37,600 --> 00:09:39,120
The advantage is clearly mine.

193
00:09:39,500 --> 00:09:40,540
Such sad prattle.

194
00:09:40,720 --> 00:09:44,840
We both know the only spirit even suitable to be Yamai's successor is me.

195
00:09:45,200 --> 00:09:47,440
Negative. I am the one who will persevere.

196
00:09:47,440 --> 00:09:50,140
The name Yamai does not fit one as lowly as you.

197
00:09:50,340 --> 00:09:54,400
Your words are hollow. My future devil side has already shown me the inevitable end.

198
00:09:54,640 --> 00:09:58,780
It gave me a vision of you, Yuzuru, impaled and dying on the end of my Sturm Lanza.

199
00:09:59,100 --> 00:10:02,260
Refute. Your devil side has never been accurate in the slightest.

200
00:10:03,040 --> 00:10:06,460
Shut up! It has so worked before! And don't you dare make fun of me!

201
00:10:06,700 --> 00:10:08,200
Shin, can you hear me?

202
00:10:08,700 --> 00:10:09,120
Reina?

203
00:10:09,740 --> 00:10:11,460
Good. I finally got through.

204
00:10:11,460 --> 00:10:13,460
Where are you in Toka currently?

205
00:10:14,140 --> 00:10:15,440
Um, not sure.

206
00:10:15,680 --> 00:10:20,500
Request. Kaguya, please provide information regarding the combat capabilities of your Sturm Lanza.

207
00:10:20,660 --> 00:10:25,440
Ha! The very font of language dries up trying to describe the scope of its awesome power.

208
00:10:25,740 --> 00:10:28,260
Tangible yet intangible. Visible yet unseen.

209
00:10:28,500 --> 00:10:30,800
Only able to sate its thirst with stabbing and piercing.

210
00:10:31,360 --> 00:10:33,880
Summary. Just like you, it is devoid of meaning.

211
00:10:34,060 --> 00:10:35,920
That's not true! It does have meaning!

212
00:10:36,120 --> 00:10:38,160
Maybe you're just too stupid to really understand!

213
00:10:38,160 --> 00:10:41,140
Derisive. Your Sturm Lanza is laughable.

214
00:10:41,560 --> 00:10:42,920
Huh. How dare you!

215
00:10:43,080 --> 00:10:47,580
To punish you for such insolence, perhaps I should rip that smirk off your face right here and now!

216
00:10:50,740 --> 00:10:52,580
We're gonna get caught in the middle!

217
00:10:52,820 --> 00:10:54,100
Stink into darkness!

218
00:10:54,580 --> 00:10:56,160
Torque. Hi-ya!

219
00:10:57,840 --> 00:10:58,660
Stomp-a!

220
00:11:00,780 --> 00:11:01,300
Huh?

221
00:11:04,740 --> 00:11:06,140
Wait, is that a human?

222
00:11:06,140 --> 00:11:09,000
Wondrous. I cannot suppress my surprise.

223
00:11:09,560 --> 00:11:10,720
Uh, hi?

224
00:11:11,340 --> 00:11:15,600
Why have you brought our sacred duel to a standstill, human? And what are your intentions for us?

225
00:11:15,740 --> 00:11:21,740
Depending on your answer, I'll, uh, turn your body into a jelly with my shot in Lanza!

226
00:11:22,120 --> 00:11:24,340
Discrepancy. Your weapon's name has changed completely.

227
00:11:24,720 --> 00:11:26,580
Unimportant! Now be quiet already!

228
00:11:26,580 --> 00:11:30,540
Query, since you are the one who was confused, why must I be quiet?

229
00:11:30,540 --> 00:11:36,920
At this rate, we won't resolve anything. Unless...

230
00:11:36,920 --> 00:11:41,860
I think I know how we can settle things. For good.

231
00:11:42,720 --> 00:11:44,900
Question. What did you have in mind?

232
00:11:45,100 --> 00:11:47,680
A new trial. We've had many contests, haven't we?

233
00:11:47,860 --> 00:11:54,000
We've each had 25 victories and come to a draw 49 times. The list of events to compete in is rapidly dwindling.

234
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:58,540
However, there is still one competition which hasn't yet determined a victor between us.

235
00:11:58,660 --> 00:11:59,880
Doubtful. Explain.

236
00:12:03,160 --> 00:12:03,360
Hm.

237
00:12:07,760 --> 00:12:08,320
Huh?

238
00:12:12,280 --> 00:12:13,960
Hey, uh, we're back.

239
00:12:15,840 --> 00:12:20,000
There's no denying. I'm obviously more lively and charming than she is.

240
00:12:20,180 --> 00:12:22,140
Seduction. I'm more fully developed.

241
00:12:22,140 --> 00:12:24,660
What gives?

242
00:12:25,020 --> 00:12:26,200
Their transfer students.

243
00:12:26,860 --> 00:12:31,080
This is highly unorthodox. The school never informed me they were coming.

244
00:12:31,260 --> 00:12:35,020
It was so sudden, they were probably worried that they couldn't contact you in time.

245
00:12:35,400 --> 00:12:37,740
Don't worry about the new girls. Leave them to me, okay?

246
00:12:38,100 --> 00:12:40,180
Please focus your energy on the other students.

247
00:12:40,300 --> 00:12:41,800
Oh, thank you.

248
00:12:42,340 --> 00:12:45,840
So, Shido, all you have to do is make a simple little choice.

249
00:12:45,840 --> 00:12:51,280
Just say, Kaguya, you drive me wild. Let me give myself to you, body and soul, forever.

250
00:12:51,500 --> 00:12:57,340
Wrong. Kaguya is a poor choice. She is quite needy and childish. However, I would strongly recommend me.

251
00:12:57,960 --> 00:12:59,620
Feeling a little smothered, are we?

252
00:13:00,580 --> 00:13:01,060
Yeah.

253
00:13:02,060 --> 00:13:12,420
Putting our feminine wiles to the test. We haven't tried that yet. Surely the true heir of the hurricane child, Yamai, would possess enough grace and charm to make all of creation quake in jealousy.

254
00:13:12,620 --> 00:13:18,560
Reply, I believe I follow your logic. In truth, it may be the only attribute which we have not put to a competition.

255
00:13:19,040 --> 00:13:23,980
Yuzuru, do you agree to pit our beauty against one another? Of course, my victory is certain.

256
00:13:24,500 --> 00:13:31,180
Negative. There is no chance that you could ever beat me. After all, I am the cutest. To be frank, your looks are average at best.

